{
  "kanji": "話",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 話\ntitle: talk, speak\njlpt: 5\ntags: [jlpt-n5, grade-2, compound, starter]\nstrokes: 13\nradical: 言\nradicalNumber: 149\nonyomi: [ワ]\nkunyomi: [はな.す, はなし]\ndistractors: [読, 書, 聞]\n---\n\n# 話 — talk, speak\n\n**Strokes:** 13 · **Key (radical):** 言 (as 訁, no. 149) · **Phonetic:** none in modern form (old 𠯑) · **JLPT:** N5 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n話 is 言 (words, speech) plus 𠯑, an old sound component. In the modern form the right-hand part looks like 舌 (tongue) only because the shapes merged graphically.\nAs a labelled mnemonic only, \"words from the tongue\" is easy to remember.\nIt means \"talk\", \"speak\" and \"a story, a conversation\".\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ワ | on | [会話](../words/会話.md) かいわ, 電話 でんわ, 話題 わだい, 神話 しんわ |\n| はな.す | kun | [話す](../words/話す.md) はなす, 話し方 はなしかた, 話し合う はなしあう |\n| はなし | kun | 話 はなし (a talk, story): 話を聞く, 面白い話 おもしろいはなし |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [話す](../words/話す.md) はなす — to speak, to talk\n- [会話](../words/会話.md) かいわ — conversation\n- 電話 でんわ — telephone\n\n## Notes\n\n- 話す takes the person with に or と: 友達と話す (talk with a friend), 先生に話す (tell the teacher). The noun 話 (はなし) is the same word without the final す.\n- 話す is a regular godan verb: 話します, 話さない, 話して, 話した.\n- Contrast: 言う いう (say), 話す (talk) and 語る かたる (narrate, a formal verb).\n- Look-alikes: [読](読.md) and [書](書.md), which are also sound-and-sense kanji, and 活 (life; with 氵 and 舌). 話 ends in 舌 (a 千-like top over 口).\n",
